   "text": "The SMILES below was read from the drawing and checked for validity by hand; I did not run it through a parser.\n\n**Macrocycle.** The ring closes through the Glu side chain: its \u03b3\u2011carbonyl is joined to a 1,4\u2011diaminobutane (putrescine) linker, which in turn is acylated by the Trp carbonyl. I counted four CH2 groups in the linker. The residues run Glu \u2192 His \u2192 4\u2011fluoro\u2011Phe \u2192 Arg \u2192 Trp, and the Glu \u03b1\u2011NH carries the 3\u2011phenylpropanoyl cap.\n\n**Stereochemistry.** I assigned each \u03b1\u2011carbon from its wedge or hash bond and the CIP priorities (N > C(=O) > side chain > H):\n- Glu is S (L).\n- His is S (L).\n- 4\u2011Fluoro\u2011Phe is R, so it is the D\u2011residue.\n- Arg is S (L).\n- Trp is S (L).\n\nSMILES: O=C(CCc1ccccc1)N[C@H]1CCC(=O)NCCCCNC(=O)[C@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccccc23)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCNC(=N)N)NC(=O)[C@@H](Cc2ccc(F)cc2)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc2c[nH]cn2)NC1=O"
